e and the approximate double bottom with 2357.18, weakening the Always-In Long read and supporting a larger trading range 2357.18-2850.", "Range development: five or more further bars overlapping inside 2633.31-2786.81 without a new high would turn the pause into a trading range at the highs and lower Always-In relevance."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790380799999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["24 bars of two-sided trade after the 2850 high is long for a simple bull flag, and the range drifts slightly lower: bar 96 close 2738.87 to bar 119 close 2690.56 is -48.31, and bar 110's 2633.31 undercuts bar 105's 2648.49 with no immediate new high.", "Lower highs after the high (2850, then 2795, 2804.59, 2786.81, 2740.42) fit an mtr-like lower-high sequence rather than fresh bull strength.", "The same window contains a -12% bear leg (2680 to 2358.62), so upside continuation is not the only structure this market has produced recently.", "Roughly half the window (the 33-bar early range plus the 27-bar post-high range) is two-sided, which is also consistent with a large trading range rather than a continuing trend."], "evidence_for": ["Window-level higher highs and higher lows: 2411.04 (bar 27 low), 2358.62 (bar 58 low), 2568.16 (bar 86 pullback low), 2850 (bar 92 high), with the close 2690.56 above the 2479.17 open.", "Spike-and-channel bull structure: bars 75-76 close 2578.60 (high 2585.5) and 2636.28 (high 2643.52), immediately followed by continuation into 2850; the 2568.16 pullback low held above the prior structure lows.", "The pullback from 2850 is about half of the final leg (2568.16-2850, 50% about 2709.08), a normal bull-channel pullback depth rather than a structure break.", "Bars 93-119 stay inside a bounded band (2804.59 to 2633.31) with overlapping bodies and mid-bar closes, which is consistent with a range phase and balanced near-term directional pressure.", "Bars 110-119 compress into 2633.31-2740.42 with mostly small ranges, a breakout-mode condition after a strong bull leg."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window opens at 2479.17 (open_time 1788652800000) and closes 2690.56 on the final bar (open_time 1790366400000), a net gain across 120 closed H4 bars.", "Bars 0-32 (1788652800000-1789127999999) overlap between 2411.04 (bar 27 low) and 2528.8 (bar 6 high) with no sustained directional closes.", "Bar 33 (1789128000000) spikes to 2680 but closes 2555.52, below its midpoint 2562.095; the market then sells to 2358.62 (bar 58, 1789488000000), about -12% from that spike high.", "Bars 57-64 lows are 2390.73, 2358.62, 2381, 2388.06, 2393.36, 2384.56, 2384.29, 2370.54: a two-sided base with a slightly higher retest low at 2370.54 rather than a clean new low.", "From 2358.62 (bar 58) the market rallies to 2850 (bar 92, 1789977600000), about +21%; bars 75-76 (1789732800000, 1789747200000) are bull spike bars closing 2578.60 and 2636.28 near their highs, and bar 86 (1789891200000) pulls back only to 2568.16 before continuation.", "Bar 92 spikes to 2850 and closes 2723.15, below its midpoint 2754.03; subsequent highs are 2795 (bar 93), 2770.03 (bar 94), 2804.59 (bar 95), 2786.81 (bar 103) and 2740.42 (bar 116), with no close above 2786.81 afterwards.", "Bars 93-119 form a bounded two-sided range: highest high 2804.59, lowest low 2633.31 (bar 110, 1790236800000), which undercuts bar 105's 2648.49; net change from bar 96 close 2738.87 to close 2690.56 is -48.31.", "Bars 110-119 compress between 2633.31 and 2740.42 with mostly sub-30-point ranges, overlapping bodies and mid-bar closes: a tight breakout-mode compression after a strong bull leg.", "The pullback from 2850 has retraced just over half of the final leg 2568.16-2850 (50% level about 2709.08) while staying far above the 2568.16 higher low."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "